    RASSF10   %TPM>1   0.0%  median  0.00  SD  0.03

== 7. Verdict against the pre-set gate =========================
  PROCEED  : >= 70% of lines at TPM >= 1, SD >= 0.5, tied < 40%
  MARGINAL : 40-70% detected, or SD 0.3-0.5
  STOP     : < 40% detected, or SD < 0.3

  RASSF9: STOP
    detected 3.5% of 113 lines | SD 0.31 | tied 26.5% | median 0.02 (log2 TPM+1)
    -> a methylation-expression correlation in these lines would be
       computed largely on the detection floor. Report as inadequate.

  RASSF10: STOP
    detected 1.8% of 113 lines | SD 0.21 | tied 18.6% | median 0.04 (log2 TPM+1)
    -> a methylation-expression correlation in these lines would be
       computed largely on the detection floor. Report as inadequate.

  WHAT THIS CANNOT SAY: this is a feasibility check on expression only.
  A PROCEED verdict does not mean the methylation data covers the RASSF9
  promoter, which is a separate question answered in step 2. A STOP
  verdict is informative in its own right: it is consistent with the
  bulk-tumour RASSF9 signal in TCGA being substantially non-malignant in
  origin, which is what our Tirosh analysis already indicated.

